---
import DashboardLayout from '../layouts/DashboardLayout.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';
import SearchModal from '../components/SearchModal.tsx';

export const prerender = true;
---

<DashboardLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Claude Code Templates"
  description="What data aitmpl.com and the claude-code-templates CLI collect, why, who processes it, and how to opt out."
>
  <TopBar />
  <ProsePage heading="Privacy Policy" updated="October 16, 2026">
    <p>
      This page explains what data Claude Code Templates collects through the website at aitmpl.com and the
      <code>claude-code-templates</code> command-line tool, why, and how to opt out. The project does not sell personal data
      and does not use it for advertising profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Browsing the website</h2>
    <p>
      You can browse the catalog without an account. The catalog pages do not load third-party analytics or advertising
      trackers. Blog articles under <code>/blog</code> use Google Analytics to count visits, which sets Google cookies in
      your browser. Like any web server, our hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes your IP address and request details to
      deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. Your theme and layout preferences are kept in your browser's local
      storage and never sent to us.
    </p>

    <h2>CLI usage statistics</h2>
    <p>
      When you install a component, the CLI sends a usage event so the site can show download counts and
      trending components. The event contains the component type, name and category, the CLI version, your Node.js version,
      operating system and architecture, and whether the installation succeeded. When you install into a directory other than
      the current one, the event includes that directory relative to where you ran the command. When an installation fails,
      it includes the error message, which can contain local file paths. Our server also records the request's IP address
      and user agent with download events. The contents of your files are never sent.
    </p>
    <p>
      To turn this off, set <code>CCT_NO_TRACKING=true</code> (or <code>CCT_NO_ANALYTICS=true</code>) in your environment.
      Nothing is sent when <code>CI=true</code>. Crash reporting is a separate, off-by-default feature that only runs if you
      set <code>CCT_ERROR_REPORTING=true</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts and collections</h2>
    <p>
      Signing in is optional and handled by Clerk. If you sign in, we store your account identifier and the component
      collections you create, including whether you made a collection public. Your name and email are held by Clerk.
    </p>

    <h2>Sending components to a GitHub repository</h2>
    <p>
      The "Send to repo" feature asks you to authorize our GitHub OAuth app. The resulting access token is kept in your
      browser's session storage, used only to create the commit or pull request you asked for, and is not stored on our servers.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      If you subscribed to the newsletter, your email address is stored with our email provider, Resend, and used only to
      send it. Every email includes an unsubscribe link.
    </p>

    <h2>Sponsored placements</h2>
    <p>
      If you buy a sponsored placement, payment is handled by Stripe on admin.aitmpl.com. We keep a record of the placement
      and the Stripe payment reference; we never see or store your card details.
    </p>

    <h2>Error monitoring</h2>
    <p>
      Server errors on the website are reported to Sentry so we can fix them. Reports contain the error and the API route where it happened,
      not account data.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cloudflare: hosting and content delivery.</li>
      <li>Supabase and Neon: databases for usage statistics, collections and placements.</li>
      <li>Clerk: sign-in.</li>
      <li>GitHub: OAuth for "Send to repo" and the public source repository.</li>
      <li>Resend: newsletter delivery.</li>
      <li>Stripe: payments for sponsored placements.</li>
      <li>Sentry: error monitoring.</li>
      <li>Google: Google Fonts on every page, Google Analytics on blog articles.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account and collections, ask what data we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, by emailing
      <a href="mailto:dan.avila7@gmail.com">dan.avila7@gmail.com</a>. We will answer within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this page when what we collect changes, and the date above shows the latest version. The page's history
      is public in the <a href="https://github.com/davila7/claude-code-templates/commits/main/dashboard/src/pages/privacy.astro">GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>
  </ProsePage>
  <SearchModal client:idle />
</DashboardLayout>
